Entries marked "—" are topics outside the scope of this series; see the Radiopaedia and MR-TIP links above.

<<<md>>>
## 3. Vendor names for the same thing

Each manufacturer has its own trade names. The physics is the same; only the label differs. (Trade names change over time and between software versions — when in doubt, check the MR-TIP comparison tables linked at the top.)

| Concept | Siemens Healthineers | GE HealthCare | Philips | Explained in |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Spoiled gradient echo | FLASH | SPGR | T1-FFE | [[H2]] |
| Fast (turbo) spoiled GRE, often IR-prepared | TurboFLASH | FSPGR / FGRE | TFE | [[H2]] |
| Unspoiled (refocused) steady-state GRE | FISP | GRASS | FFE | [[H2]] |
| Reversed (echo) SSFP | PSIF | SSFP | T2-FFE | [[H2]] |
| Balanced SSFP | TrueFISP | FIESTA | Balanced FFE (bFFE) | [[H2]] |
| Fast/turbo spin echo (RARE) | TSE | FSE | TSE | [[H2]] |
| Single-shot (half-Fourier) FSE | HASTE | SSFSE | SSh-TSE (single-shot TSE) | [[H2]] |
| 3D FSE with variable flip angles | SPACE | CUBE | VISTA | [[H2]] |
| 3D IR-prepared $T_1$w GRE brain | MPRAGE | BRAVO (3D IR-FSPGR) | 3D TFE ($T_1$-TFE) | [[H2]] |
| 3D fat-suppressed $T_1$w GRE (body) | VIBE | LAVA | THRIVE | [[H1]] |
| Fat–water separation | Dixon | IDEAL / FLEX | mDIXON | [[D2]] |
| Susceptibility-weighted imaging | SWI | SWAN | SWIp | [[D2]] |
| Radial ("blade") motion-robust FSE | BLADE | PROPELLER | MultiVane | [[I2]] |
| Parallel imaging, image domain | mSENSE | ASSET | SENSE | [[H3]] |
| Parallel imaging, k-space | GRAPPA | ARC | — (SENSE used) | [[H3]] |
| Simultaneous multislice | SMS (Simultaneous Multi-Slice) | HyperBand | MultiBand SENSE | [[H3]] |
| Compressed sensing | Compressed Sensing (CS) | HyperSense | Compressed SENSE | [[H3]] |
| Deep-learning reconstruction | Deep Resolve | AIR Recon DL | SmartSpeed | [[H3]] |
| Partial Fourier | Partial Fourier | fractional NEX / partial echo | Halfscan / partial echo | [[H3]] |
| Number of averages | Averages | NEX | NSA | [[G2]] |
| Echo train length | Turbo factor | ETL | TSE factor | [[H2]] |
| Receiver bandwidth specified as | Hz/pixel | ±kHz (half the total BW) | water–fat shift (pixels) | [[G3]] |
| Spectral fat saturation | FatSat, SPAIR | Fat Sat (ChemSat), SPECIAL, ASPIR | SPIR, SPAIR | [[D2]] |

> **⚠️ Common confusion:** the original book's Fast Imaging chapter lists Philips' FSE as "turbo field-echo (TFE)". That is incorrect: Philips calls fast spin echo **TSE** (turbo spin echo); **TFE** (turbo field echo) is Philips' fast *gradient-echo* family (used e.g. for MPRAGE-type scans).

> **⚠️ Common confusion:** GE quotes bandwidth as "±31.25 kHz", i.e. *half* the total readout bandwidth (62.5 kHz). Siemens' "Hz/pixel" is the total bandwidth divided by the number of readout samples. Philips' "water–fat shift" in pixels is the fat displacement $|\Delta f_{cs}|/(BW/\text{pixel})$. The cell below converts between the three.

<<<code>>>
def bandwidth_conventions(total_bw_hz, n_read, B0):
    """Express one readout bandwidth in the three vendor conventions."""
    per_pixel = total_bw_hz / n_read                          # Siemens: Hz/pixel
    ge_half = total_bw_hz / 2                                 # GE: +/- kHz
    wfs = abs(mt.ppm_to_hz(mt.FAT_SHIFT_PPM, B0)) / per_pixel  # Philips: water-fat shift [pixels]
    return per_pixel, ge_half, wfs

for bw, n, B0 in [(62.5e3, 256, 1.5), (62.5e3, 256, 3.0), (250e3, 128, 3.0)]:
    pp, half, wfs = bandwidth_conventions(bw, n, B0)
    print(f"total BW {bw/1e3:6.1f} kHz, N_read = {n}, B0 = {B0} T  ->  "
          f"Siemens {pp:6.0f} Hz/px | GE +/-{half/1e3:6.2f} kHz | Philips WFS {wfs:4.2f} px")

<<<md>>>
Interpretation: the same 62.5 kHz readout is "244 Hz/px" (Siemens), "±31.25 kHz" (GE) and "0.9 px water–fat shift at 1.5 T / 1.8 px at 3 T" (Philips). The very wide EPI-like bandwidth in the last line pushes the fat shift far below one pixel along the readout.

<<<md>>>
## Key takeaways

* Each glossary entry links to the chapter where the concept is explained — use it as a jumping-off point.
* Many acronyms are vendor trade names for the same physics: FLASH = SPGR = T1-FFE, TrueFISP = FIESTA = bFFE, TSE = FSE, MPRAGE ≈ BRAVO ≈ 3D TFE, GRAPPA ≈ ARC, mSENSE ≈ ASSET ≈ SENSE.
* Some acronyms collide (ADC, GE, PC): always spell out at first use.

